    "full_teaching_text": "2- Dimensioning:\r\n\r\nOne of Grasshopper's most powerful tools is dimensioning. Having the geometry, we are now able to choose specific elements and dimension them parametrically.\r\n\r\nIn this case, the process is very simple:\r\n1- We need to dimension the triangles in the square grid.\r\n2- Therefore, we need to find their edges (this is the element of each triangle to be dimensioned)\r\n3- \"Deconstruct Brep\" provides all edges.\r\n4- \"Curve Length\" provies all curve lengths.\r\nUsing the previously found Function that reduces the decimal places, we can control the numbers.\r\n5- \"End Points\" provides all curves end points, snapping the dimension lines.\r\n6- \"Aligned Dimension\" is the main component generating the dimensions.\r\n7- Check the other dimension components under the Tabs\r\n\"Display\" > \"Dimensions\"",
